    state itself: the state summary immediately before every frame
    must equal its recorded ``before`` (the first frame's must equal
    the bound checkpoint checksum), and the summary immediately
    after must equal its recorded ``after``. Renumbering or
    rebuilding the prev chain after swapping, duplicating or
    reordering frames therefore cannot hide the tampering: frames
    would describe state transitions the replayed business state does
    not take.
